+It is not a process model. It is the baseline the process models
+(\code{\link[=cogmod_lnr]{cogmod_lnr()}}, \code{\link[=cogmod_rdm]{cogmod_rdm()}}, \code{\link[=cogmod_ddm]{cogmod_ddm()}}, \code{\link[=cogmod_lba2]{cogmod_lba2()}}) can be
+measured against: it takes the same \code{rt | dec(response)} data, so
+\code{brms::loo_compare()} puts it side by side with them, and the difference
+says how much a sequential sampling model gains over the analysis most
+people run by default.
+
+Functions:
+\itemize{
+\item \code{rcogmod_gaussbit()}: Simulates random draws.
+\item \code{dcogmod_gaussbit()}: Computes the density (likelihood).
+\item \code{cogmod_gaussbit()}: Creates a \code{brms::custom_family()}.
+\item \code{cogmod_gaussbit_stanvars()}: Generates the \code{stanvars} to pass to \code{brm()}.
